)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}]}],"michaelisConstants":[{"constant":1.7,"unit":"mM","substrate":"Gly-Phe-pNA (at pH 8 and 37 degrees Celsius)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}]},{"constant":0.87,"unit":"mM","substrate":"Ala-Ala-pNA (at pH 8 and 37 degrees Celsius)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}]},{"constant":7.2,"unit":"mM","substrate":"Gly-Phe-beta-naphthylamine (at pH 8 and 37 degrees Celsius)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}]}]},"phDependence":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}],"value":"Optimum pH is 8 for the hydrolysis of Gly-Phe-pNA."}]},"temperatureDependence":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}],"value":"Optimum temperature is approximately 30 degrees Celsius for the hydrolysis of Gly-Phe-pNA. Stable at a temperature below 20 degrees Celsius for 30 minutes."}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24827749"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}],"value":"Homodimer"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24827749"}],"value":"The chymotrypsin fold (25-276 and 574-722) is the catalytic domain and the alpha-helical domain (277-573) is the regulatory domain necessary for exopeptidase activity"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"24827749"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"8892831"}],"value":"Designing engineered forms of this protein with the ability to produce custom dipeptides potentially may have a number of commercial and industrial uses including food industry (PubMed:24827749, PubMed:8892831). Maybe useful for drug design (PubMed:24827749)"}],"commentT